.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.8181818181818182, "x1": 0.6164835164835165, "y1": 0.8313908313908314}, {"text": "(i) Find the value of k.", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.83993783993784, "x1": 0.3747252747252747, "y1": 0.8648018648018648}, {"text": "(ii) How many more years will elapse before only 30% of the original", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.8756798756798757, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}, {"text": "amount remains?", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.8896658896658897, "x1": 0.35824175824175825, "y1": 0.8997668997668997}], [{"text": "QUESTION 7. Use a separate Writing Booklet. Marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.09712509712509712}, {"text": "(a) A factory assembles torches. Each torch requires one battery and one bulb. It is 2", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.12665112665112666, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.13986013986013987}, {"text": "known that 6% of all batteries and 4% of all bulbs are defective.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.14063714063714064, "x1": 0.667032967032967, "y1": 0.15073815073815075}, {"text": "Find the probability that, in a torch selected at random, both the battery and the", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.1825951825951826}, {"text": "bulb are NOT defective. Give your answer in exact form.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.18337218337218336, "x1": 0.6186813186813187, "y1": 0.19658119658119658}, {"text": "(b) A Y B", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.22688422688422688, "x1": 0.6175824175824176, "y1": 0.23853923853923853}, {"text": "ABCD is a parallelogram. The point X lies on CD, the point \u00a5 lies on AB, and", "x0": 0.16593406593406593, "y0": 0.34654234654234656, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.3714063714063714}, {"text": "AX = CY = BC, as shown in the diagram.", "x0": 0.16923076923076924, "y0": 0.36752136752136755, "x1": 0.4978021978021978, "y1": 0.38073038073038074}, {"text": "(i) Copy the diagram into your Writing Booklet.", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.3947163947163947, "x1": 0.5813186813186814, "y1": 0.40792540792540793}, {"text": "(ii) Explain why ZADX = ZCBY.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.42424242424242425, "x1": 0.46593406593406594, "y1": 0.43745143745143744}, {"text": "(iii) Show that AD = AX.", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.45143745143745145, "x1": 0.38461538461538464, "y1": 0.46386946386946387}, {"text": "(iv) Show that triangles ADX and CBY are congruent.", "x0": 0.17912087912087912, "y0": 0.4801864801864802, "x1": 0.610989010989011, "y1": 0.4933954933954934}, {"text": "Hence prove that AYCX is a parallelogram.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.5097125097125097, "x1": 0.5593406593406594, "y1": 0.5221445221445221}, {"text": "(\u00a9)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5524475524475524, "x1": 0.14065934065934066, "y1": 0.5641025641025641}, {"text": "Level of", "x0": 0.2923076923076923, "y0": 0.5944055944055944, "x1": 0.36043956043956044, "y1": 0.6045066045066045}, {"text": "pollutant", "x0": 0.29010989010989013, "y0": 0.60994560994561, "x1": 0.36153846153846153, "y1": 0.6223776223776224}, {"text": "1945 1995", "x0": 0.3626373626373626, "y0": 0.6728826728826729, "x1": 0.6692307692307692, "y1": 0.6822066822066822}, {"text": "Time", "x0": 0.510989010989011, "y0": 0.6884226884226884, "x1": 0.5527472527472528, "y1": 0.6977466977466977}, {"text": "The graph shows the levels of a pollutant in the atmosphere over the past 50", "x0": 0.16593406593406593, "y0": 0.7257187257187258, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.7389277389277389}, {"text": "years.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.7435897435897436, "x1": 0.21208791208791208, "y1": 0.7536907536907537}, {"text": "Describe briefly how the level of this pollutant has changed over this period of", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.7684537684537684, "x1": 0.8054945054945055, "y1": 0.7816627816627817}, {"text": "time. Include mention of the rate of change.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.7832167832167832, "x1": 0.512087912087912, "y1": 0.7964257964257965}], [{"text": "QUESTION 7. (Continued)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.34615384615384615, "y1": 0.09634809634809635}, {"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8186813186813187, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.0947940947940948}, {"text": "Given that log, b = 2-75 and log, c = 0-25, find the value of:", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.128982128982129, "x1": 0.6527472527472528, "y1": 0.14219114219114218}, {"text": "(d)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.12975912975912976, "x1": 0.14175824175824175, "y1": 0.1414141414141414}, {"text": "@", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.17249417249417248, "x1": 0.2043956043956044, "y1": 0.18414918414918416}, {"text": "(ii)", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.21056721056721056, "x1": 0.2043956043956044, "y1": 0.2222222222222222}, {"text": "QUESTION 8. Use a separate Writing Booklet.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2828282828282828, "x1": 0.512087912087912, "y1": 0.29603729603729606}, {"text": "Greg and Jack are playing in a golf tournament. They will play two rounds and", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.32556332556332557, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.33877233877233875}, {"text": "(a)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.32634032634032634, "x1": 0.14065934065934066, "y1": 0.337995337995338}, {"text": "each has an equal chance of winning the first round.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.34032634032634035, "x1": 0.5747252747252747, "y1": 0.35353535353535354}, {"text": "If Greg wins the first round, his probability of winning the second round is", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.3682983682983683, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.3815073815073815}, {"text": "increased to 0-6.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.38306138306138304, "x1": 0.2945054945054945, "y1": 0.39316239316239315}, {"text": "If Greg loses the first round, his probability of winning the second round is", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.411033411033411, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.42424242424242425}, {"text": "reduced to 0-3.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.42657342657342656, "x1": 0.2824175824175824, "y1": 0.4358974358974359}, {"text": "(Draw a tree diagram for the two-round sequence. Label each branch of", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.45376845376845376, "x1": 0.8054945054945055, "y1": 0.466977466977467}, {"text": "the diagram with the appropriate probability.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.46853146853146854, "x1": 0.5725274725274725, "y1": 0.48174048174048173}, {"text": "(ii) Find the probability that Greg wins exactly one round.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.4965034965034965, "x1": 0.6516483516483517, "y1": 0.5097125097125097}, {"text": "On I July 1985, Anna invested $10 000 in a bank account that paid interest at a", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.5361305361305362, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.5563325563325563}, {"text": "(b)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.54001554001554, "x1": 0.14175824175824175, "y1": 0.5516705516705517}, {"text": "fixed rate of 8% per annum, compounded annually.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.554001554001554, "x1": 0.5703296703296703, "y1": 0.5672105672105672}, {"text": "(i) How much would be in the account after the payment of interest on", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.581973581973582, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.5951825951825952}, {"text": "1 July 1995 if no additional deposits were made?", "x0": 0.22857142857142856, "y0": 0.5967365967365967, "x1": 0.610989010989011, "y1": 0.60994560994561}, {"text": "(ii) In fact, Anna added $1000 to her account on | July each year, beginning", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6247086247086248, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.6379176379176379}, {"text": "on | July 1986.", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.6402486402486403, "x1": 0.34835164835164834, "y1": 0.6526806526806527}, {"text": "How much was in her account on I July 1995 after the payment of", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.6674436674436675, "x1": 0.8054945054945055, "y1": 0.6806526806526807}, {"text": "interest and her deposit?", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.6822066822066822, "x1": 0.4164835164835165, "y1": 0.6954156954156954}, {"text": "(iii) Anna\u2019s friend, Jennifer, invested $10 000 in an account at another bank", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.7101787101787101, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.7226107226107226}, {"text": "on | July 1985 and made no further deposits. On 1 July 1995, the", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.7249417249417249, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.7381507381507382}, {"text": "balance of Jennifer's account was $35 478.", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.7389277389277389, "x1": 0.5681318681318681, "y1": 0.7498057498057498}, {"text": "What was the annual rate of compound interest paid on", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.7676767676767676, "x1": 0.7120879120879121, "y1": 0.7808857808857809}, {"text": "account?", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.7824397824397824, "x1": 0.2934065934065934, "y1": 0.7917637917637917}], [{"text": "10", "x0": 0.4901098901098901, "y0": 0.04195804195804196, "x1": 0.5065934065934066, "y1": 0.05128205128205128}, {"text": "QUESTION 9. Use a separate Writing Booklet. Marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.09712509712509712}, {"text": "(a) 7", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.12742812742812742, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.13908313908313907}, {"text": "A rectangular beam of width w cm and depth d cm is cut from a cylindrical pine", "x0": 0.16263736263736264, "y0": 0.331002331002331, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.3543123543123543}, {"text": "log as shown.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.35275835275835277, "x1": 0.27362637362637365, "y1": 0.3651903651903652}, {"text": "The diameter of the cross-section of the log (and hence the diagonal of the cross-", "x0": 0.16593406593406593, "y0": 0.38073038073038074, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.3939393939393939}, {"text": "section of the beam) is 15 cm.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.3947163947163947, "x1": 0.4021978021978022, "y1": 0.40714840714840717}, {"text": "The strength S of the beam is proportional to the product of its width and the", "x0": 0.16593406593406593, "y0": 0.4234654234654235, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.4366744366744367}, {"text": "square of its depth, so that", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.43745143745143744, "x1": 0.37252747252747254, "y1": 0.4506604506604507}, {"text": "(i) Show that $= K(225w -", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.49417249417249415, "x1": 0.4197802197802198, "y1": 0.5213675213675214}, {"text": "(i) What numerical dimensions will give a beam of maximum strength?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5361305361305362, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.5493395493395493}, {"text": "Justify your answer.", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.5501165501165501, "x1": 0.38461538461538464, "y1": 0.5633255633255633}, {"text": "(ii) A square beam with diagonal 15 cm could have been cut from the log.", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.5788655788655789, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.5920745920745921}, {"text": "Show that the rectangular beam of maximum strength is more than 8%", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.5928515928515928, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.6060606060606061}, {"text": "stronger than this square beam.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.6076146076146076, "x1": 0.4703296703296703, "y1": 0.62004662004662}, {"text": "(b) 5", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6503496503496503, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.662004662004662}, {"text": "v", "x0": 0.2164835164835165, "y0": 0.655011655011655, "x1": 0.22417582417582418, "y1": 0.6612276612276612}, {"text": "(velocity)", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6658896658896659, "x1": 0.25934065934065936, "y1": 0.6783216783216783}, {"text": "10 t (time)", "x0": 0.6571428571428571, "y0": 0.7987567987567987, "x1": 0.7846153846153846, "y1": 0.8111888111888111}, {"text": "A particle is observed as it moves in a straight line in the period between t = 0", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.8453768453768454, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.8648018648018648}, {"text": "and r=10. Its velocity v at time ris shown on the graph above.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.8624708624708625, "x1": 0.6648351648351648, "y1": 0.8756798756798757}], [{"text": "QUESTION 9. (Continued) Marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08469308469308469, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.09634809634809635}, {"text": "Copy or trace this graph into your Writing Booklet.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.12665112665112666, "x1": 0.5725274725274725, "y1": 0.13986013986013987}, {"text": "On the time axis, mark and clearly label with the letter Z the times when", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.15151515151515152, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.1717171717171717}, {"text": "the acceleration of the particle is zero.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.5197802197802198, "y1": 0.1825951825951826}, {"text": "(ii) On the time axis, mark and clearly label with the letter G the time when", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.19735819735819735, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.21056721056721056}, {"text": "the acceleration is greatest.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.21212121212121213, "x1": 0.432967032967033, "y1": 0.22533022533022534}, {"text": "(iii) There are three occasions when the particle is at rest, ie.", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.24164724164724163, "x1": 0.6945054945054945, "y1": 0.25485625485625485}, {"text": "and", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.2564102564102564, "x1": 0.25274725274725274, "y1": 0.26573426573426573}, {"text": "The particle is furthest from its initial position on one of these occasions.", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.28438228438228436, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.2975912975912976}, {"text": "Indicate which occasion, giving reasons for your answer.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.29836829836829837, "x1": 0.6703296703296703, "y1": 0.31157731157731156}, {"text": "QUESTION 10. Use a separate Writing Booklet.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3682983682983683, "x1": 0.521978021978022, "y1": 0.3815073815073815}, {"text": "(a) Draw the graphs of y = 4cosx and y", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.411033411033411, "x1": 0.5164835164835165, "y1": 0.42424242424242425}, {"text": "\u2014xon the same set of axes for 3", "x0": 0.5560439560439561, "y0": 0.411033411033411, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.4226884226884227}, {"text": "(i) Explain why all the solutions of the equation 4cos.x=2\u2014x must lie", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.4560994560994561, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.4693084693084693}, {"text": "between x=~2 and x=6.", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.47086247086247085, "x1": 0.43956043956043955, "y1": 0.48096348096348096}, {"text": "(b) Two particles A and B start moving on the x axis at time t= 0. The position of 9", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5050505050505051, "x1": 0.8747252747252747, "y1": 0.5283605283605284}, {"text": "particle A at time is given by", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.5236985236985237, "x1": 0.3967032967032967, "y1": 0.5431235431235432}, {"text": "and the position of particle B at time ris given by", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.5858585858585859, "x1": 0.5494505494505495, "y1": 0.5990675990675991}, {"text": "x= 4sint.", "x0": 0.4736263736263736, "y0": 0.6177156177156177, "x1": 0.5527472527472528, "y1": 0.627039627039627}, {"text": "(i) Find expressions for the velocities of the two particles.", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.6441336441336442, "x1": 0.6538461538461539, "y1": 0.6573426573426573}, {"text": "(ii) Use part (a) to show that there are exactly two occasions, t, and when", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6728826728826729, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.6876456876456877}, {"text": "these particles have the same velocity.", "x0": 0.22637362637362637, "y0": 0.6891996891996892, "x1": 0.5197802197802198, "y1": 0.7024087024087025}, {"text": "(iii) Show that the distance travelled by particle A between these two", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.717948717948718, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.7311577311577312}, {"text": "occasions is", "x0": 0.22527472527472528, "y0": 0.7319347319347319, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.7420357420357421}, {"text": "(iv) Show that the two particles never meet.", "x0": 0.17912087912087912, "y0": 0.7902097902097902, "x1": 0.5285714285714286, "y1": 0.8034188034188035}], [{"text": "12", "x0": 0.4901098901098901, "y0": 0.04195804195804196, "x1": 0.5065934065934066, "y1": 0.05128205128205128}, {"text": "STANDARD INTEGRALS", "x0": 0.378021978021978, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.6164835164835165, "y1": 0.09401709401709402}, {"text": "x\"de net: x40, ifn<o", "x0": 0.2857142857142857, "y0": 0.1250971250971251, "x1": 0.7285714285714285, "y1": 0.13675213675213677}, {"text": "\u201cn+l", "x0": 0.42857142857142855, "y0": 0.1320901320901321, "x1": 0.48131868131868133, "y1": 0.14607614607614608}, {"text": "dx =Inx, x>0", "x0": 0.3021978021978022, "y0": 0.1895881895881896, "x1": 0.5351648351648352, "y1": 0.20124320124320125}, {"text": "dy", "x0": 0.3142857142857143, "y0": 0.2533022533022533, "x1": 0.33296703296703295, "y1": 0.2634032634032634}, {"text": "1", "x0": 0.44945054945054946, "y0": 0.30924630924630925, "x1": 0.45274725274725275, "y1": 0.3185703185703186}, {"text": "cosax dx =~sinax, a#0", "x0": 0.2857142857142857, "y0": 0.3146853146853147, "x1": 0.5681318681318681, "y1": 0.3356643356643357}, {"text": "a", "x0": 0.4461538461538462, "y0": 0.33255633255633255, "x1": 0.45604395604395603, "y1": 0.33877233877233875}, {"text": "1", "x0": 0.46263736263736266, "y0": 0.37373737373737376, "x1": 0.46703296703296704, "y1": 0.38306138306138304}, {"text": "sinaxdx =-\u2014cosax, a#0", "x0": 0.2857142857142857, "y0": 0.3815073815073815, "x1":